Moose blocks road. Driver panics. Carstrikes tree. Tree owner threatens to sue.You spend three hours in teleconferencewith your legal advisors.The Gravel Act of 1973 specifically forbadethe use of gravel on the tundra. When usedas a building material, gravel makes thepermafrost melt more quickly.30Huskies are wonderful guard dogs. Theyare also very friendly. An informant's dogbowls you over and you lose one hourwhile he licks your face.Pundits called the purchase of Alaska fromRussia "Seward's Folly." They believed theterritory was just a distant icebox thatwould drain America's finances.11A totem pole artist offers to carve andpaint your life story. You spend two hourswatching yourself be immortalized in cedar. The energy released by the Good FridayEarthquake has been estimated to be10,000,000 times stronger than the atomicbomb dropped on Hiroshima.21A Native rights demonstration closes downall transportation facilities. Even ardentsupporters of their cause are stranded for three hours.The first act of the first session of the firstAlaskan territorial legislature in 1913 wasapproval of women's voting rights - sevenyears before universal suffrage in the USA.31A sourdough recommends the Hickel Highway.A trusting soul, you take it - a big mistake!The road resembles a trench; even your all-terrain taxi becomes stuck. You lose two hours.When Flow Station Two was scrapped at a costof $2-3 million, it nearly bankruptedAlyeska. Many environmentalists hoped thiscrisis would stop the pipeline.20You stop to see a Native culture display.Clues are everywhere! The blanket tossersselect you to participate. You spend an hoursailing skyward and falling toward earth.The "Rondy" is a snowmobile race aroundAlaska, but it doesn't visit the entire state.After the start in Anchorage, it loops throughNome and Barrow and finishes in Fairbanks.10You enter a cafe intending to call Lazar.Inside 50 happy pipeliners celebrate payday.They accost you. For two hours you hearnothing but tall tales and laughter."To drag up" is a phrase used on the pipeline.It means to move, after an undesired jobtransfer further north, to another worksite.20Your snowmobile sinks into a drift, so youput on your snowshoes. After slogging backto town, you're hot under the collar butcold everywhere else. You lose two hours.During WWII, Japanese planes bombed theUS navy base at Dutch Harbor. Later, enemytroops attacked Kiska Island in the Aleutiansand briefly occupied Nome.20You ride a dog sled to follow up a lead, whena herd of caribou crosses your path. Yourstartled dogs go off in the wrong direction,and you pull into town three hours late.A sudden shock can liquify Anchorage's soil -it is thixotropic. The condition occurs whencertain minerals are missing.31Dr. Know calls you for a change! He knowsa lot, but can't move a refrigerator alone.You want to stay in his good graces, soyou drop everything. It takes two hours.One week before it was to receive an AllAmerican Cities Award, Seward wasdestroyed by a horrible avalanche.20